      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right to be cautious about using electronic countermeasures, as it may trigger the system's diagnostic sensors. A passive approach to neutralizing the pulsed signal is to use a carefully calibrated resonant frequency, tuned to the carrier wave's frequency, but offset by a small margin. This technique, known as \"frequency hopping\" or \"frequency scrambling,\" can disrupt the coherence of the carrier wave and render it incoherent, making it less effective. However, this method requires a deep understanding of the carrier wave's frequency and phase characteristics, as well as precise control over the resonant frequency.",
